Reproducible in: v4.0-stable, v4.4-stable, v4.5-dev(1-5), v4.5-beta1\n\nEarliest reproducible version: [v4.5-beta2](https://godotengine.org/download/archive/4.5-beta2/)\n\n### System information\n\nGodot v4.6.stable - Windows 11 (build 26200) - Multi-window, 2 monitors - Direct3D 12 (Forward+) - dedicated NVIDIA GeForce RTX 4070 (NVIDIA; 32.0.15.8097) - AMD Ryzen 7 7700X 8-Core Processor (16 threads) - 31.14 GiB memory\n\n### Issue description\n\n[Here](https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=DzWu7lK2AO4) is a video demo of the bug.\n\nWhen using an 8BitDo Ultimate 2 controller, putting the controller to sleep (either by letting it sit idle for long enough or by placing it back on the charging dock) causes the Godot editor to go unresponsive.\n\nWaking the controller back up does not resolve the bug. The editor remains unresponsive.\nIn Godot versions 4.0-stable through 4.5-beta1, the editor seems to lag/freeze for a half a second when the controller is docked and undocked, but not fully go unresponsive.\nIn case it is related to the bug, I am using the 8BitDo Ultimate Software V2 version 1.29. \n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\n1. Connect an 8BitDo Ultimate 2 controller to your computer. Ensure that Godot recognizes inputs from the controller.\n2. Allow the controller to go to sleep by letting it sit idle long enough for the LED ring to turn off or by placing it back on the charging dock.\n3. This should cause the engine to stop responding.\n\n### Minimal reproduction project (MRP)\n\nN/A","closed_by":{"login":"Repiteo","id":17489292,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3NDg5Mjky","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/17489292?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo","html_url":"https://github.com/Repiteo","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/u